    "patternFlow": "Pattern: Two Pointers\nTemplate:\nlo, hi = 0, n - 1\nwhile lo < hi:\n  if good(lo, hi): record; move both or one\n  elif too_small: lo += 1\n  else: hi -= 1\n\nApply to \"Valid Palindrome\": maintain the pattern's state while scanning, update the answer whenever the window/structure is valid.",
    "important": "Shows you discard half the search space without nested loops. Say: “Sorted + pair → two pointers from both ends.”",
