    "question": "You are given an integer array height of length n. There are n vertical lines. Find two lines that together with the x-axis form a container that holds the most water. Return the maximum amount of water.",
    "example": "Example 1:\nInput: height = [1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]\nOutput: 49\nExplanation: lines at index 1 (h=8) and 8 (h=7) → width 7 → area 7*7=49.",
    "thinking": "Area = min(h[lo], h[hi]) * (hi−lo). Brute all pairs O(n²). Two pointers: start widest; move the shorter wall inward — only a taller wall can improve area.",
    "explain": "## Intuition\nThe water level is limited by the shorter line. If you move the taller line, the width shrinks and the height cannot increase past the short one — area cannot improve. So always move the shorter pointer.\n\n## Walkthrough\nStart lo=0, hi=n-1. Compute area, then if height[lo] < height[hi] do lo++, else hi--. Track max.\n\n## Proof sketch\nAny pair skipped by moving the short wall is dominated by a wider container with the same limiting height.",
    "naiveApproach": "Check every (i,j) pair — O(n²).",
    "optimizedApproach": "Two pointers from both ends — O(n).",
    "patternFlow": "lo=0 hi=n-1 best=0\nwhile lo<hi:\n  best = max(best, min(h[lo],h[hi])*(hi-lo))\n  if h[lo] < h[hi]: lo++ else hi--",
    "important": "Move the shorter wall. Equal heights: move either (or both).",
    "snippetJava": "int area = Math.min(h[lo], h[hi]) * (hi - lo);\nif (h[lo] < h[hi]) lo++; else hi--;",
    "snippetPython": "area = min(h[lo], h[hi]) * (hi - lo)\nif h[lo] < h[hi]: lo += 1\nelse: hi -= 1",
    "java": "class Solution {\n    public int maxArea(int[] height) {\n        int lo = 0, hi = height.length - 1, best = 0;\n        while (lo < hi) {\n            best = Math.max(best, Math.min(height[lo], height[hi]) * (hi - lo));\n            if (height[lo] < height[hi]) lo++;\n            else hi--;\n        }\n        return best;\n    }\n}",
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def maxArea(self, height: List[int]) -> int:\n        lo, hi = 0, len(height) - 1\n        best = 0\n        while lo < hi:\n            best = max(best, min(height[lo], height[hi]) * (hi - lo))\n            if height[lo] < height[hi]:\n                lo += 1\n            else:\n                hi -= 1\n        return best",
    "complexity": "Time O(n), Space O(1)",
    "followUp": "Trapping Rain Water is related but needs leftMax/rightMax or stack.",
    "tip": "One line: “Move the shorter wall.”",
    "edgeCases": [
      "n=2",
      "Strictly increasing",
      "All equal heights"
    ]
