    "example": "Example 1:\nInput: n = 2\nOutput: 2\n1+1 or 2\n\nExample 2:\nInput: n = 3\nOutput: 3\n1+1+1, 1+2, 2+1",
    "thinking": "To reach step n you came from n−1 or n−2. So ways(n)=ways(n−1)+ways(n−2). Fibonacci with base ways(1)=1, ways(2)=2.",
    "explain": "## Intuition\nEvery path to n ends with a single step from n−1 or a double step from n−2. Those sets of paths are disjoint and cover everything → recurrence.\n\n## Build bottom-up\na=1 (n=1), b=2 (n=2). For i=3..n: a,b = b, a+b.\n\n## Interview tip\nMention recursion + memo first, then optimize to two variables.",
    "naiveApproach": "Pure recursion exponential time.",
    "optimizedApproach": "O(n) DP or O(1) rolling variables.",
